WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:05.900
Good afternoon.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:06.850
Good afternoon, internet.

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:08.740
We're gonna try and
implode this drum today.

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:10.660
Veritasium did a cool video where

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:11.710
you heat up some water inside,

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:13.790
you turn it all to steam, you bung it up,

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:14.623
you cool it down,

00:00:14.623 --> 00:00:16.860
and the pressure causes it
just to implode on itself.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.500
I made a barbecue thingy here earlier.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.130
Sort of half assed it, didn't
bother doing the rest of it.

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:23.960
We're gonna heat it up on there,

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:24.900
with some water in,

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.490
and then move it to here

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:28.480
and then cool it down in
some cold water and a hose

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:30.200
and hopefully we get the implosion effect.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.810
We're gonna try to film the implosion

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:34.480
at two and a half
thousand frames a second.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.953
And see if it looks all
graceful and crinkly.

00:00:39.459 --> 00:00:40.530
Are you confident about this experiment,

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:41.480
think it will work?

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:44.513
I recon we're gonna try.

00:00:46.001 --> 00:00:47.150
I don't know, I'll be
surprised if it worked.

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:48.251
Really?

00:00:48.251 --> 00:00:49.335
I'll be surprised if we can do it.

00:00:50.738 --> 00:00:51.571
Yeah.

00:00:51.571 --> 00:00:52.520
With our lack of experience.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:54.422
Looks like it's kicking off
some right steam there, Dan.

00:00:54.422 --> 00:00:55.620
Yeah, it is, it's working right.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:56.810
I think we're ready.

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:57.643
Okay.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:00.760
You know what to do.

00:01:03.044 --> 00:01:03.877
Whoa.

00:01:15.267 --> 00:01:16.890
Aw, Damn, it's gone, this side.

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:17.723
Oh!

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:19.940
Go, .

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:23.510
Alright, Dan, we appear to have suffered

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:24.700
a partial implosion.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:25.840
We did.

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:26.673
Hold your hand there

00:01:26.673 --> 00:01:27.750
where that's gonna be again.

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:30.333
Oh.

00:01:30.333 --> 00:01:31.583
It's exploding now.

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:33.283
And you've bummed it already?

00:01:33.283 --> 00:01:34.392
Yeah.
Okay.

00:01:34.392 --> 00:01:35.340
Oh,

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:36.730
Oh, God!

00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:37.563
Ow!

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:39.253
Whoo!

00:01:44.755 --> 00:01:45.770
Oh, it did it!

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:46.790
Yeah.

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:48.363
It totally did it.

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:54.790
Ooh!

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:56.230
That happened really quickly.

00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:58.330
You can see, there, the water
hasn't even started moving--

00:01:58.330 --> 00:01:59.163
You can see how quickly it went

00:01:59.163 --> 00:02:00.290
because the water sat on top.

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:01.123
Yeah.

00:02:01.123 --> 00:02:02.670
It just got whipped out from under it.

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:03.503
Yeah.

00:02:03.503 --> 00:02:04.421
That is mental.

00:02:04.421 --> 00:02:05.583
It's a really cool experiment.

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:08.230
That guy agrees.

00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:10.654
Well, that was really
impressive, actually,

